# gitleaks fingerprint allowlist (doc/standards/04). One `commit:path:rule:line`
# fingerprint per line, each with a comment stating why it is a false positive.
# The hooks scan the working tree (no commit prefix); a run that scans history
# reports the same finding with a commit-qualified fingerprint, which is added
# beside the plain one when it appears.
#
# The PUBLIC stock default database_encryption_key that Ludus ships in its own
# source (badsectorlabs/ludus, ludus-api/config.go). The role compares the live
# key against it to refuse operating on an uninitialised store; it is not a
# credential.
roles/cluster_ludus_auth/defaults/main.yml:generic-api-key:6
